The fastest land animal in the world is the cheetah.

Here is the extended C# code to implement the CSV export feature while maintaining the existing functionality:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;

public class SummaryReport
{
    public string Title { get; set; }
    public string Content { get; set; }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        return $"Title: {Title}\nContent: {Content}";
    }
}

public class ReportGenerator
{
    public void GenerateReport(SummaryReport report, bool exportToCsv = false, string csvFilePath = null)
    {
        // Existing functionality: Output summary report to console
        Console.WriteLine("Report Summary:");
        Console.WriteLine(report.ToString());

        // Additional feature: Export report in CSV format if requested
        if (exportToCsv)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(csvFilePath))
            {
                csvFilePath = "report.csv";
            }

            try
            {
                using (var writer = new StreamWriter(csvFilePath, false, Encoding.UTF8))
                {
                    // Write CSV header
                    writer.WriteLine("Title,Content");

                    // Write report data, escaping commas and quotes in content
                    string escapedContent = report.Content.Replace("\"", "\"\"");
                    writer.WriteLine($"\"{report.Title}\",\"{escapedContent}\"");
                }

                Console.WriteLine($"Report exported to CSV: {csvFilePath}");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error exporting to CSV: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
1. **Existing Functionality Preserved**: The method still prints the report summary to the console.
2. **CSV Export Feature**:
   - Added optional parameters `exportToCsv` (bool) and `csvFilePath` (string) to control CSV export.
   - If `exportToCsv` is `true`, the report is written to a CSV file.
   - The CSV file includes a header row (`Title,Content`) and properly escapes special characters (commas and quotes) in the content.
   - Error handling is included to catch and report any issues during file writing.
